  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Cities Investment Facility</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Cities Investment Facility (CIF) Programme is a public/private, multi-stakeholder, multi-stage initiative established by UN-Habitat to address the Urban infrastructure development gap while ensuring and certifying the furtherance of the 17 Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs). The programme unlocks private investment in urban infrastructure projects within low- and middle-income markets. 
 
The Cities Investment Facility (CIF) is centred around unlocking greater capital flows to urban impact projects, by supporting their processes of ideation, design, financing, and implementation, using a series of partnership-based instruments. CIF aims to direct up to USD$1.8 billion of capital towards financing projects that are inclusive, gender-responsive, masterplan-integrated, and align with UN-Habitat&#x2019;s existing geographical footprint. It is anticipated that CIF will provide technical assistance to up to 28 urban projects by 2028 .</narrative>
  </description>
